  "behaviour": [
    "One queue (Redis + BullMQ, conventions.md) with a database record of every job and every run; nothing timed depends on a page being open.",
    "Open at the moment: at opensAt the wish link starts returning content (the link also checks server time on every read, so a late job never opens early or late).",
    "Rest at term end, erase 365 days after resting, end of the 30-day restore window, erase-now within 24 hours, reminders and notices, Pass/plan/creator periods, Vault billing, royalties, reconciliation.",
    "Jobs are idempotent: re-running a job for the same subject and due time changes nothing twice. Failed jobs retry with backoff, then go dead and show to ops.",
    "A daily sweep re-schedules any due transition missing from the queue (the database is the truth, the queue is a cache)."
  ],
